).","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","title":"isPlanar","identifier":"doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/isPlanar","url":"\/documentation\/planarity\/graphprotocols\/graph\/isplanar","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Planarity/documentation/Planarity/GraphProtocols/Graph/findKuratowskiSubgraph()":{"abstract":[{"text":"A subdivision of K₅ or K₃,₃ made of the graph’s edges, or nil when the graph is planar: the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"witness of non-planarity. A dense graph is searched on its first 3n − 5 distinct pairs only,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"which already hold one. O(n + m).","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/planarity\/graphprotocols\/graph\/findkuratowskisubgraph()","identifier":"doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/findKuratowskiSubgraph()","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"findKuratowskiSubgraph","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"KuratowskiSubgraph","preciseIdentifier":"s:9Planarity18KuratowskiSubgraphV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">?","kind":"text"}],"title":"findKuratowskiSubgraph()"},"doc://Planarity/documentation/Planarity/GraphProtocols/Graph":{"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Graph"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Planarity on undirected graphs. Self-loops and parallel edges never change an answer: the tests"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"run on the underlying simple graph, read once through the rows in index space. A directed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"graph’s planarity is that of "},{"code":"graph.undirectedView","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"extension"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P","text":"Graph"}],"url":"\/documentation\/planarity\/graphprotocols\/graph","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","title":"Graph","role":"symbol"},"doc://Planarity/documentation/Planarity/GraphProtocols/Graph/planarEmbedding()":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/planarity\/graphprotocols\/graph\/planarembedding()","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"planarEmbedding","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PlanarEmbedding","preciseIdentifier":"s:9Planarity15PlanarEmbeddingV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">?","kind":"text"}],"title":"planarEmbedding()","identifier":"doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/planarEmbedding()","abstract":[{"text":"A planar embedding of the graph, over every edge position (loops and parallel copies","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"included), or nil when the graph is not planar: the witness of planarity. O(n + m), faces","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"included.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Planarity/documentation/Planarity":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity","role":"collection","title":"Planarity","url":"\/documentation\/planarity"},"doc://Planarity/documentation/Planarity/GraphProtocols/Graph/isOuterplanar":{"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Whether the graph has a planar embedding with every vertex on one face: whether the graph","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"plus a new vertex joined to every vertex is planar. A simple graph with more than 2n − 3","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"edges is not. O(n + m).","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity\/GraphP